CM_ BO_ 81 "VCM->GENE MCU composite command. 100 Hz, DLC=6. B0 purpose unknown. B5 = rolling counter 0x00-0x0F.";
CM_ SG_ 81 gen_torque_cmd "Positive = motoring (engine cranking). Negative = generating. Null at engine off.";
CM_ SG_ 81 gen_rpm_ref "Null when engine off (raw=0x7FFF). Zone+fine encoding: B4 is zone selector (127=null, 130-135=active, 256 RPM/zone); B3 is fine RPM within zone. Bit-for-bit identical to 0x052 B2-B3.";

CM_ BO_ 1041 "BMS-sourced (drops when HV battery LV connector unplugged). 16 Hz, DLC=8. High-resolution SoC register. Remaining bytes encode a contactor request signal (changes at startup, not shutdown; not decoded). NOT in EPRI plist.";
CM_ SG_ 1041 bms_soc_hires "Valid during startup before 0x596 becomes non-zero.";

CM_ BO_ 1136 "NOT in EPRI DBC. POST_CONTACTOR HV bus voltage -- drops to ~3V when contactors open (HVAC pull), no further change on HVD pull. Source ECU unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 1136 hv_bus_volt_470 "Byte layout assumed symmetric with 0x482 -- not independently verified from Ghidra.";

CM_ BO_ 1426 "VCM-sourced. 100 Hz, DLC=8. B2-B3=throttle position (this DBC). Brake pedal (B4-B5) and switch flags (B0) are in epri-pt-bus.dbc. B1 role unconfirmed.";
CM_ SG_ 1426 throttle_pos "Scale to physical % unconfirmed.";

CM_ BO_ 1430 "BMS-sourced (drops when HV battery LV connector unplugged). ~1 Hz. Integer SoC percent at B6. NOT in EPRI plist.";
CM_ SG_ 1430 bms_soc "Integer-rounded version of 0x411. Use 0x411 for sub-percent resolution.";

CM_ BO_ 1432 "VCM/HCU-sourced. ~1 Hz, DLC=8. Power statistics for ESS, generator, and traction channels. All three are offset-binary excess-32768 (zero at raw 0x8000), 0.01 kW/count. Sign convention: positive = providing energy to HV bus. Channel balance trac_power = ess_power + gen_power holds. B6-B7 = static bias, not power data. ESS and traction channels are stubbed in epri-pt-bus.dbc -- the EPRI app decodes them as plain signed int16 and is wrong. FILTERING DIFFERS BY CHANNEL: ess_power and trac_power are ~8 s rolling averages (the -Avg- in the EPRI names is literal); gen_power is instantaneous. This is why gen_power matches measured V*I far better than the other two -- it is a filtering difference, not a decode error. Confirmed 2026-08-02 by sweeping a moving-average window over measured V*I and re-correlating.";
CM_ SG_ 1432 ess_power "Battery pack power. Positive = battery discharging; negative = charging/regen. Active during AC charging; near-zero when the generator fully covers traction load. Encoding corrected from the EPRI app's signed-int16 decode. TIME-AVERAGED, not instantaneous: agreement with measured 0x410 pack V*I peaks at a ~8 s boxcar-equivalent filter (r 0.807 raw -> 0.984 at 8 s). Do not use for energy integration -- use 0x410 pack V*I.";
CM_ SG_ 1432 gen_power "Near-zero in pure EV mode. Positive = generator providing power to HV bus. Not decoded by the EPRI app at all. INSTANTANEOUS, unlike the other two channels: matches measured 0x482 GENE V*I at r=0.9998 / 209 W mean error against a -5.2..+55.6 kW swing, and any smoothing makes agreement worse. Appears to be a direct passthrough of the 0x482 V*I product. Observed operating range is wider than that validation window: the 2026-07-24..26 weekend trip exercises the signal to 142.8 kW with no sign of saturation or wrap, consistent with a genset rated near 150 kW. Note the channel balance trac_power = ess_power + gen_power breaks transiently by -55..-75 kW during fast ramps -- that is the documented filtering difference (ess/trac are ~8 s rolling averages, gen is instantaneous), not a decode error.";
CM_ SG_ 1432 trac_power "Drivetrain power. Positive = traction motor consuming power from the HV bus; negative = regen. Large in both EV and hybrid operation. Encoding corrected from the EPRI app's signed-int16 decode. TIME-AVERAGED, not instantaneous: agreement with measured 0x462 TRAC V*I peaks at a ~8 s boxcar-equivalent filter (r 0.794 raw -> 0.916 at 8 s). Do not use for energy integration -- use 0x462 TRAC V*I.";

CM_ BO_ 1604 "VCM-sourced (part of VCU cluster 0x639-0x64B). 100 Hz. Cruise control diagnostic -- VCM internal cruise state and speed setpoint. NOTE: NOT a command to the traction inverter (TRAC MCU is on the OBD bus). Signals reflect VCM cruise logic state for diagnostic/monitoring only.";
CM_ SG_ 1604 cruise_mode "0x8=idle/standby, 0x9=throttle override/auto-disengage, 0xA=active cruise (speed controller running).";
CM_ SG_ 1604 cruise_speed_setpoint "Zero when inactive. 1 km/h per button press.";

CM_ BO_ 776 "BorgWarner TCM. 100 Hz, DLC=5. B0=ParkRequest/ParkPinState in epri-pt-bus.dbc. B1-B2=InputShaftSpeed (this DBC). B3-B4=constant 0x00. Cross-vehicle: identical encoding on Coda (CODA-D-CAN.dbc). See notes/borgwarner.md.";
CM_ SG_ 776 InputShaftSpeed "Zero=0x7D80 at rest. Input shaft (not output): ratio vs trac_rpm is 2.000 regardless of gear ratio, matching on both Vtrux and Coda.";

CM_ BO_ 1442 "VCU-sourced re-broadcast of traction motor speed and torque. ~100 Hz, DLC=8. B0-B1 and B6-B7 uncharacterized. See notes/powertrain-messages.md.";
CM_ SG_ 1442 trac_rpm "Scale assumed 1 RPM/count by symmetry with GENE_RotSpd (0x054) and TRAC_RotSpd (0x044). Positive = forward rotation.";
CM_ SG_ 1442 trac_torque_fbk "Positive = motoring; regen = negative. Scale to physical Nm unconfirmed.";

CM_ BO_ 1609 "VCU/VCM evap canister purge control. 0x649 on PT bus, ~20 Hz, VCU-sourced. Full message encoding differs between drive and charge modes -- byte fields repurpose themselves; values cannot be compared across modes. B0 role UNRESOLVED: it was previously mapped as the evap-active flag (bit 7) and that mapping is now invalidated -- see notes/evap-cycle-analysis.md Phase 5. B1 role unresolved. B2 upper nibble is a free-running clock independent of evap state.";
CM_ SG_ 1609 vcm_evap_active "B4 bit 7. 1 = evap cycle pending or purging; 0 = not pending. Set at key-on when a cycle is due, before the engine ever runs, and clears at VCM-declared completion (~6.1s before the generator is commanded to stop). Holds through involuntary stalls -- tracks VCM intent, not engine state. Verified across all 104 logged sessions containing 0x649: set in 17/17 sessions where a purge actually ran, never set spuriously. NOTE: this flag alone does not distinguish PENDING from PURGING -- pair it with vcm_evap_counter (0 = pending, >0 = purging).";
CM_ SG_ 1609 vcm_evap_counter "12-bit purge progress counter: B2 lower nibble = MSB, B3 = LSB. 0 whenever no cycle is active. Counts up only while the engine is running during an active evap cycle; frozen when the engine stops (stall or controlled off) and resumes on restart; survives log gaps and key cycles within a cycle. Returns to 0 at completion. Rate is variable (~0.1-1.0 counts/s, ramps up then down) and the terminal value differs per cycle (observed 901, 901, 856), so this is NOT a percentage and cannot drive a progress bar. Use only as a zero/non-zero purging discriminator.";

CM_ BO_ 1593 "VCM-sourced (part of VCU cluster 0x639-0x64B). 100 Hz, DLC=8. Carries the shift lever position the VCM has resolved from the Via shifter position box. B2-B3 active but uninterpreted; B5 near-constant 0x48/0x49. See notes/shifting-transfer-case-investigation.md.";
CM_ SG_ 1593 shift_lever_pos "B6 bits[6:4]. Confirmed against logs/generator-on-then-off.log (steps 3->4 at t=39.08s and 4->3 at t=53.26s, matching the documented M engagement held ~14s) and logs/vtrux_shifter_disconnect.log (drops to 2=Neutral the instant the shifter box is unplugged at t=20.30s, returns on reconnect at t=29.56s -- the VCM's documented Neutral safe default). 0x644 B0 bits[7:6] carries the same index but only 2 bits, so it cannot distinguish M from Park; use this signal.";

CM_ BO_ 1594 "VCM-sourced (part of VCU cluster 0x639-0x64B). 100 Hz, DLC=8. No confirmed signals. B6-B7 are the generator initialization state described in notes/status-bits-cross-log-comparison.md. B7 observed values: 0x04, 0xC4, 0xD4, 0xE4, 0xF4; bits[3:0] constant 0x4. B7 bits[5:4] form a 2-bit field taking all four values: generator related, not further characterized. Use 0x649 for evap. See notes/powertrain-messages.md and notes/evap-cycle-analysis.md.";

CM_ BO_ 1606 "VCM-sourced (part of VCU cluster 0x639-0x64B). 100 Hz, DLC=8. Carries the Via amber warning telltale state. This is a Via system and is unrelated to the GM/GMLAN telltale set. See notes/warning-lamp-investigation.md.";
CM_ SG_ 1606 via_warn_lamp_state "B7 bits[6:4]. 0 = HV not up (pre-start OR shut down by a major HV fault -- ambiguous on its own, pair with 0x400 B0 or 0x410 B1). 6 = HV up, lamp off. 5 = HV up, lamp ON. Bit6 set whenever HV is up; bit5 and bit4 are mutually exclusive, so effectively bit5=normal, bit4=warning. IMPORTANT: B7 bit7 is a separate 1 Hz heartbeat -- mask it off, or the raw byte (0x60/0xE0 normal, 0x50/0xD0 lit) looks like it is toggling. Does NOT encode a blinking lamp: during major HV faults the field goes to 0 rather than oscillating.";

CM_ BO_ 2248146946 "VCU-sourced extended frame (29-bit). Re-broadcasts traction motor thermal load from OBD bus. B5/B6 carry trac_therm_ind_pct; other bytes uncharacterized (B0 multiples of 4, B3 slow 5-value field, B1[7:6] rolling sub-counter). See notes/thermal-investigation.md.";
CM_ SG_ 2248146946 trac_therm_ind_pct "VCU re-broadcasts from OBD bus 0x44A B2 as integer percent. Traction derate onset ~78-79%. B5[1:0] are ADC jitter.";

CM_ BO_ 2289188935 "Sanden HV AC compressor (SA=0x47) EAC_STATUS2. DLC=4. Broadcasts at exactly 10 Hz regardless of compressor state (on, off, charging). Synchronized pair with 0x0868A047 (EAC_STATUS1). See notes/hvac-investigation.md.";
CM_ SG_ 2289188935 eac_hv_input "B2=0 before HV contactors close. EPRI-named EAC_CompHVInput.";



CM_ BO_ 2566849312 "(SA=0x20). EMP WP29 C20 PE glycol coolant pump. J1939 proprietary PGN 0xFF03. Tier: Pump CAN (independent of BMS and 12V tiers). ~1 Hz. No signals decoded. Sole ID attributed to SA=0x20.";

VAL_ 1604 cruise_mode 8 "idle_standby" 9 "throttle_override" 10 "active";

VAL_ 1609 vcm_evap_active 0 "not_pending" 1 "pending_or_purging";

VAL_ 1593 shift_lever_pos 0 "Park" 1 "Reverse" 2 "Neutral" 3 "Drive" 4 "Manual_generator_mode";


VAL_ 1606 via_warn_lamp_state 0 "hv_not_up" 5 "lamp_on" 6 "lamp_off";

